@DeMoorJasper I've fixed the tests, all of them pass (according to CI, not Windows Node 12, but that seems like a bug to me).

Right now, the transformer is almost at 1:1 feature parity with `vue-loader` (just a few things, like custom block support, are missing). However, for the VAST majority of use cases, the current feature set will do.

I'm also wondering if making the transformer configurable (say with a `.vuerc`) would be useful.

I've added support for custom blocks but the syntax is quite different from Webpack's `vue-loader`.

In the Vue config (`.vuerc`, `vue.config.js`, etc.):
```json
{
    "customBlocks": {
        "docs": "./src/docs-preprocessor.js"
    }
}
```
In `src/docs-preprocessor.js`:
```js
export default function(component, blockContent, blockAttrs) {
    if (blockAttrs.brief)
        component.__briefDocs = blockContent;
    else
        component.__docs = blockContent;
}
```
In any Vue component (say `HomePage.vue`):
```vue
<template>
  <div>Home Page</div>
</template>

<docs>
This component represents the home page of the application.
</docs>

<docs brief>
Home Page
</docs>
```
In a parent component (say `App.vue`):
```vue
<template>
  <div>
    <child></child>
    docs: {{docs.standard}}
    in brief: {{docs.brief}}
  </div>
</template>

<script>
import Child from './HomePage';
export default {
  components: {
    child: Child
  },
  data() {
    return {
      docs: {
        standard: Child.__docs,
        brief: Child.__docsBrief
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

At this point, the transformer has full feature parity with `vue-loader` and is ready for merging. Not sure why the macOS CI is failing on HMR since I didn't really touch the core at all; assume it's a bug? @DeMoorJasper @mischnic

@101arrowz the CI is probably a new bug either discovered or caused by this PR.
Might look into it later.
The PR in general looks really good.

issue_context.body:
What the issue's title says.

It can lead to very confusing bugs, for example your imports stop being what they should be, but only in production build, etc.

I think it's enough to change `src/assets/VueAsset.js`
```js
    let supplemental = `
      var ${optsVar} = exports.default || module.exports;
      if (typeof ${optsVar} === 'function') {
        ${optsVar} = ${optsVar}.options;
      }
    `;

    supplemental += this.compileTemplate(generated, scopeId, optsVar);
    supplemental += this.compileCSSModules(generated, optsVar);
    supplemental += this.compileHMR(generated, optsVar);
```
to
```js
    let supplemental = `
      (function(exports, module){
      var ${optsVar} = exports.default || module.exports;
      if (typeof ${optsVar} === 'function') {
        ${optsVar} = ${optsVar}.options;
      }
    `;

    supplemental += this.compileTemplate(generated, scopeId, optsVar);
    supplemental += this.compileCSSModules(generated, optsVar);
    supplemental += this.compileHMR(generated, optsVar);
    supplemental += "})(exports, module);"
```
Notice the added IIFE.
